// Spitewalkers

@0 = ~Riveted Leather Boots~
@1 = ~Spitewalkers~

// @10 = ~~  // #6824
@11 = ~Forged in the infernal forges of Avernus, the Spitewalkers were originally crafted for a devilish torturer who believed that anger was the purest fuel for violence. Their dark leather is studded with tiny inward-facing barbs of infernal iron. The wearer feels a sharp sting with every step, and the pain never quite fades.

The agony slowly infects the wearer’s temperament, leaving them irritable, impatient, and constantly on edge. In combat, this manifests as a dangerous aggression: the wearer gains a bonus to melee damage and attack rolls but suffers a penalty to missile attacks, as they are too agitated to calmly aim. The constant torment also disrupts concentration, giving the wearer a chance of spell failure whenever they attempt to cast a spell.

The barbs cannot be removed without damaging the boots, and those who attempt to discard the Spitewalkers often find themselves inexplicably putting them back on, unless a Remove Curse spell is used.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Damage (melee): +2 bonus
– THAC0 (melee): +2 bonus
– THAC0 (ranged): -4 penalty
– Casting failure: 25%
– Inflicts 1d2 points of piercing damage per round while the wearer is moving during combat
– May only be removed with a Remove Curse spell

Weight: 2~

@20 = ~Pain~
